msgid "COMMAND_DESK_GUIDE_BODY"
msgstr "[font_size=18][color=#f5c747]COMMAND DESK[/color][/font_size]\n\n[color=#79d6bf]High-level intent[/color]\nChoose a commander, objective, main axis, risk posture, and reserve policy. One accepted intent assigns tasks to every deployed card still under that commander. Cards keep separate formations while acting toward the same objective.\n\n[color=#79d6bf]Automatic engagement[/color]\nCommander-controlled combat cards engage nearby threats known to their faction. Every capable member of a card shares the target, and nearby combat cards under the same commander support the engagement. Reconnaissance, withdrawing, and player-controlled cards are never pulled into combat.\n\n[color=#79d6bf]Decision queue[/color]\nThis is an exception queue, not a second command menu. It lists blocked, exposed, low-organization, low-Supply, and reinforcement conditions. The main button is currently executable; Acknowledge/Keep only accepts the risk. The receipt names the affected force, result, reason, and recovery.\n\n[color=#79d6bf]Disengage and withdraw[/color]\nDisengage cancels a commander's advance and rallies every card they still control near headquarters. A player-controlled card offers Return first. Black Well's withdrawal corridor is different: a whole card that reaches it permanently leaves that battle and preserves survivors."
